  message: "ML-STACK CARVE-OUT RETIRED in PR #1250 (6d01ea8d9f). 24 ids removed from all four lists (ci.yml, release.yml, woodpecker.yml, scripts/release-check).\n\nEvidence, 2026-09-27, live pip-audit -f json runs (records: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/totak_09272026/):\n- dev box (torch 2.14.0, transformers 5.17.0, joblib 1.5.3), NO ignores: only diskcache PYSEC-2026-2447 (alias CVE-2025-69872) and nltk PYSEC-2026-3740 fire, both fix_versions [].\n- rebuilt ci.yml/woodpecker audit env and rebuilt release.yml env (core[dev] + 4 lang pkgs + tracker + pins): neither installs torch, transformers, joblib, nltk or diskcache; each exits 0 with only the two CI ignores.\n- release-check's new audit command on the dev box exits 0.\n\nStructural: the files claimed the lists were identical / in sync and nothing checked it. tests/test_audit_ignore_lists.py now pins the three CI lists equal and release-check = CI + its two named local-only carve-outs. Mutation: adding PYSEC-2026-139 back to woodpecker.yml alone turns it red.\n\nCorrection: release-check said diskcache arrives via CairoSVG/safety; pip show says llama_cpp_python. Fixed in the comments.\n\nSTAYS OPEN per its own close condition: diskcache and nltk still have no fix.\n\nALSO SEEN, NOT ACTED ON (outside this row's defined scope, filed separately): in both rebuilt envs an audit with NO ignores at all exits 0 -- pytest 9.0.3 and pip 26.2.1 resolve, which fix the two \"permanent\" CI ignores CVE-2025-71176 and CVE-2026-3219. Not dropped here: the self-hosted runner's toolcache Python is not what I rebuilt."  # 9ec4
